  emoji: '🇮🇳',
  chapterText:
      'Before Bharati Tai became famous in our town for the small library she ran from her veranda, she had '
      'been a young schoolteacher who joined the freedom movement in the 1940s. She often told our history '
      'club about the day she decided to participate in a protest march despite knowing that teachers who '
      'joined such demonstrations risked losing their jobs immediately, and possibly their freedom as well. '
      'She said the decision had not felt brave at the time; it had simply felt necessary.\n\n'
      'During the march, the police arrived to disperse the crowd, and Bharati Tai found herself arrested '
