      'farmers, lawyers, and homemakers alike, all united by the same hope for an independent nation. She '
      'described teaching some of her fellow prisoners to read during those months, refusing to let the '
      'confinement stop her from doing the work she loved.\n\n'
      'When she was finally released, Bharati Tai found that her teaching position had indeed been given '
